t":"Wirric Stanton - one part Roman Torchwick, two parts Shou Tucker, sprinkle with Guilt Complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T06:58:18-08:00","id":1351031,"title":"","content":"Eriast, Eclipse Caste <br /> <br /> 1 whole Radames*<br /> Simmer in a light broth of Captain Jack Sparrow until at the appropriate level of wordplay.<br /> Remove, set on an oven-safe platter of A World That Hates And Fears You**, and set under the broiler until you've got a nice browning of paranoia.<br /> <br /> Remove, sprinkle with Berserk\u00ae brand Judeau, and serve <br /> <br /> * The Musical Radames is what we used in our test kitchen; while the more established Verdi Aida might be easier to find, the prevalent notes of wanderlust were critical in nailing the character arc, and our tasters also appreciated the implications of reincarnation.<br /> <br /> ** You might be tempted to use a normal world setting for the broiling, but we found that most Exalted will permanently distort whatever you put them in as they rise. We used Jade City, but that setting is long gone. Checking reviews to confirm a static setting resistant to PC-driven change is recommended in order to keep the Exaltation concealed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 11-26-2019, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T10:41:43-08:00","id":1351066,"title":"","content":"Gyoka Gyochi. One part Bruce Wayne, one part Pol Pot, one part Kira Yoshikage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I won\u00b4t even try to defend her goodness or something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T11:07:53-08:00","id":1351074,"title":"","content":"Cynis Ganan: If Luke Cage and Toph Beifong had a baby, and that baby was raised by Hannibal Lector and Malcolm X on a diet of hatred and cocaine until he was shipped off to Hogwarts where he secretly learned martial arts from Pai Mei's ghost... you'd have a reasonable approximation of Cynis Ganan. Add just a pinch of Edward Elric's insecurities and a dusting of Light Yagami (sans people skills), and the literal bloody minded nature of the MCU's Drax and you're the rest of the way there.<br /> <br /> Wow... that was a pointless excercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2